# Gate step 1141-vf9w — data, not code.
#
# Binds the HERMETIC fixture. It spawns its own marked processes and reaps
# them; it needs no podman, no toolbox and no gate, so it is honest on every
# host and costs the inner loop almost nothing.
#
# The END-TO-END demonstration is deliberately not wired: it needs a live
# toolbox and a real gate, and a gate step that launches a gate is a recursion
# nobody wants. That evidence is the transcript on 1132-r4mt and 1141-vf9w.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking a cancelled dispatch cannot leave its container-side tree running (1141-vf9w)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-dispatch-reap.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the dispatch reaper regressed (1141-vf9w) — a cancelled gate may again survive in the same checkout, or the reaper may have widened beyond its own dispatch; see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Dispatch reap check passed"

# ORDER 1141-vf9w, darwin (macbookair 2026-09-13). Exit 2 from the fixture means
# THIS PLATFORM CANNOT RUN THE ARMS — no /proc, no setsid — not that the reaper
# regressed. Without this the fixture's honest "I could not look" collapsed into
# STEP_ERROR above, which is a content verdict about a reaper the host never
# exercised, and it refused every macOS land on an otherwise green trunk
# (measured on this host: origin/linux-next c6d191d39, reproduced in a pristine
# worktree). Exit 1 remains a genuine regression and still refuses.
#
# A SKIP IS NOT COVERAGE. macOS has no working reaper today; the darwin design
# is filed as a child of this order. This field stops the gate lying in the
# other direction, it does not claim the platform is protected.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=2
STEP_SKIP_DESC="no /proc and/or no setsid on this host — the dispatch reaper is unsupported here (1141-vf9w)"
